architecture creator-channel
  canonical_name CreatorChannel
  family surface
  domain Media / Creator channel
  layer surface
  semantic_question How can a creator program compose published media into a channel without making the channel a media, rights, delivery, community, analytics or proof owner?
  purpose Native creator-channel owner. It records a channel's creator binding, visibility, Community reference, current published MediaProgram memberships and actor-specific ChannelSubscription. It compiles a Watch/Shorts/Live/Playlists/Community human surface and typed AddressPlane advertisement.
  maturity measured
  owns CreatorChannel
  owns ChannelPublication
  owns ChannelSubscription
  consumes MediaProgram
  consumes ActorClosure
  consumes Community
  publishes ChannelSurfaceProjection
  node_types CreatorChannel
  node_types ChannelPublication
  node_types ChannelSubscription
  node_types ChannelSurfaceProjection
  edge_types publishes_media_program
  edge_types subscribes_to_channel
  edge_types projects_channel_surface
  internal_calculus creator channel x currently published CMS MediaProgram x ActorClosure -> channel surface / ChannelSubscription | refusal
  invariant a ChannelPublication can reference only a current CMS MediaProgram whose subject and publication status exactly match; it never copies media identity or bytes into the channel store
  invariant external subscribe/unsubscribe derives the actor solely from the current BonfyreAuth ActorClosure; a supplied raw actor is not a public channel API
  invariant a ChannelSubscription records a bounded audience relationship only; it is not notification delivery, a social relationship authority, a playback right or a watch event
  invariant a ChannelSurface filters every listed membership through the current CMS publication state, so a later-unpublished MediaProgram disappears without the channel asserting it remains playable
  forbidden_inference a channel listing -> media ownership, a playable representation, bytes delivered, a live session, a view, a subscriber notification, comment admission, monetization, creator payment or watch proof
  source_path cmd/BonfyreChannel/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreChannel/tests/channel_test.sh
  witness cmd/BonfyreChannel/tests/channel_test.sh proves a native channel can bind only current published video/live MediaPrograms, exposes its creator-channel surface, binds subscribe/unsubscribe through a real Auth ActorClosure, refuses private-channel subscription and emits forwarding-only advertisements
  source_lineage YouTube-shaped creator grammar composed from native CMS MediaProgram, Auth ActorClosure, Community and separate MediaLibrary/MediaDelivery/MOQT owners
  known_gap upload/ingest, comments/moderation, search/recommendation, notification delivery, analytics, creator economics, HLS/DASH/MOQT delivery, live object relay, playback completion and watch proof remain distinct owners
